{
  "_README_agreedRoleFormat": {
    "note": "JSON has no comment syntax. This _-prefixed field is documentation only; Keycloak's realm import ignores unknown top-level keys, so it is safe to leave in.",
    "agreedRoleFormat_meaning": [
      "1. The claim - realm roles must appear in 'realm_access.roles' in the login token. The standard Keycloak realm-roles mapper does this and is included in this export.",
      "2. The names - the 4 workflow roles (admin / store_manager / coordinator / vhw) AND the resource roles (OPENMRS, ALL_EVENTS, MANAGE_*) must be the EXACT strings the apps expect. A role named anything else is silently ignored (user gets 403 / no permissions).",
      "3. Brokering / federation (options B, C, D) - the partner IdP groups or AD groups must be mapped onto these role names, and a mapper must emit them into 'realm_access.roles'. If the IdP sends roles in a custom claim (e.g. 'groups' or 'https://gov.ls/roles') or under different names, we add a mapper to translate them - but that mapping must be agreed up front."
    ],
    "seeAlso": "docs/keycloak-integration-options-email.md"
  },
